; This package owns the socket. The framing above it is pure and lives in
; tron-rpc; the HTTP/1.1 parser here is pure too, and separated from the flow so
; it can be driven a byte at a time -- which is how a real socket delivers, and
; where framing bugs actually live.
;
; Functorised over Mirage_flow.S rather than over an HTTP client because the
; confidential Solo5 targets forbid NET_BASIC outright and sptmac has no
; networking at all, so vsock is the only transport there. TLS wraps the flow
; rather than living here: a TLS flow is a flow.

(library
 (name tron_rpc_flow)
 (public_name tron-rpc-flow)
 (libraries tron-rpc yojson lwt cstruct mirage-flow fmt))
